Severity: WARN
Category: services
Check: check_nginx
Fix: Narrow the group to ssl-cert or root, or chmod 600.
References: ngx_http_ssl_module
Controls: CIS 3.3; NIST AC-3, SC-12; ISO 8.3, 8.24; CE User access control

The server's TLS key can be read by a group that is neither root nor
ssl-cert. Debian's ssl-cert group exists for exactly this: the key at
640 there is the done-right setup, and this finding says nothing
about it.
